<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Casimir of the Palatinate-Simmern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1543">1543</a>–<a href="/years/1592">1592</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as John Casimir, Count Palatine of Simmern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Casimir was a Calvinist prince of the Palatinate, a younger son of Elector Frederick III. He led German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> armies to aid the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a>, notably in 1567–1568 and 1575–1576, and intervened in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. From 1583 to 1592 he governed the Electoral Palatinate as regent for his nephew Frederick IV and restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calvinism">Calvinism</a> after the Lutheran reign of his brother Louis VI.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-casimir-of-the-palatinate-simmern.jpg" alt="John Casimir of the Palatinate-Simmern" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous (copy) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Casimir_(Pfalz).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
